Z||000004||JSocha||10-05-2001||12:54 AM||||Well Cheeve, I have been depressed ever since I was down in Houston and after you, your wife and I went out for supper.  No! No! No! No!  Not because I met you because that was a highlight to my trip to Houston, to be able to meet you and the Mrs. <P>I was just so tired that evening, that after supper with you guys and especially after I got back to Dallas after driving all night, I realized I had completely forgot to grab the camera and get a picture of you and the wife as was my original plan when meeting everyone.  <P>You got one of me with you, however, I didn't get one of you and your wife.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Been really bummed since that.  Brought the 35mm all that way down to Houston for that purpose and didn't use it.<P>Now our Fiscal Year End has me stressed as I am assisting to close our year end, make the required year end backups, we have a guy up from KRONOS to train us in configuring there system until tomorrow afternoon because that class was canceled when I got thrown over to FL and to get the bar coding system implemented as quickly as possible when we start the new fiscal year.  Next week booked solid with another KRONOS guy from TX who will be installing and initializing the software and importing the data to get it online.  Comes in Monday and leaves Friday of next week.<P>Then tonight, got the 86 GT back from the mechanic (bill hasn't been figured out yet...so that could depress me more once I do get it) and decided to take the passenger interior door panel off to get a head start on cleaning and lubricating the lock and door latch rod joints on that side and replace the outer dew strip to see what I'm up against.  Have that door apart and got to one of the last two screws that are behind the glass, only to loose it in the door.  Finally gave up after I realized, that to get the window out, I would have to drill out all the rivets just to get to that last little dandy of a screw so conviently placed behind the glass.  <P>Then I come in here, do a search on PFF on "dew strips" in TD&Q, only to learn Rodney Dickman created or is dealing in a tool to get to those two little dandy, well placed buggers behind the glass without having to take the glass out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>So I ordered that tonight to hopefully get it sent out tomorrow to be here by Saturday afternoon so I can get the car back together so Heidi can take it back to college with her this Sunday.<P>Then on top of all that, I'm getting withdrawl symptoms from not being able to be on PFF morning, noon and night.  I'm here so infrequently lately, that I have finally realized my wife got her hair done...while I was in FL & TX and I now have become reaquainted with what she looks like. Janice was a complete stranger to me because of all the time I typically spend here on PFF.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Who needs a TV in the bedroom?  <P>PFF is the ultimate in birth control.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>My speakers for the 86GT (Pyles) haven't been shipped yet.  Ordered them on Monday.  I thought the 4x10's in that car were removed.  Took the grill guard and removed the one on the passenger side...so it was there, just not working.  So I was going to take off the stereo brush plate, pull the radio and see if the radio harness matches the Fiero harness.  Couldn't find my set of TORX bits to use on those screws.<P>I just pick the dandiest of times to start something, late at night.<P>Have to mow my yard (and put the Fiero's in the lawn to take a picture of my lawn/Future Fiero Fountains and house to post on DJRice's thread) this weekend and drain the sprinkler system because it is getting cold.  20 - 25 degrees expected tonight.  Snow possibly this weekend.<P>So much to do...and so little time to spend here on PFF. *sigh*<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000005||Cheever3000||10-05-2001||01:34 AM||||Hey Socha:  Sorry I asked.<P><BR>Heheh, j/k!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I'm feeling better already!  Except when I think my job is the ONLY thing going right.  At least I have one, huh?<P>What, you're not going to take advantage of FOCOA's Tool Loan Program?  Yeah, right.<P>I'll have to finish that roll of film before I can get that pic to you.  <P><B>MsBeth:</B><BR>Thanks for the mail.  Every friend helps, and I knew this was the place to find em.  Thanks all of you guys for the comaraderie the past 14 months since I first came here.<BR>Enough sappy stuff, where's the dancing hamsters?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||10-05-2001||01:28 PM||||I'm almost always depressed.. but today I was talking to a guy who's selling a fiero... I tried to buy it back in july but he didn't end up selling it then because his son wanted to restore it, but the guy wanted something done with it within 2 weeks.. that was several months ago, it's still there.. so I asked him again about it, he's gonna email me tonight.. but then I'll realize how much it costs to restore a fiero that's been sitting in a field for a year.. plus insurance.. then I'll get depressed again, but at least I'd have a project fiero to work on to cheer me up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
